    "font" : "SFRM1200",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We want to study the relations between the dual group A of A and the dual groups H and A/H of the subgroup H and the quotient group A/H. In fact, one can identify A/H with the subgroup H⊥, called the annihilator of H, deﬁned as"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 3,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 209.279, 645.523, 402.719, 667.898 ],
    "font" : "CMMI12",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "H⊥ := χ ∈ A : χ(x) = 1 ∀x ∈ H ,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 4,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 70.439, 601.691, 542.645, 643.898 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1200",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "so that if we take φ ∈ L1(A) and deﬁne φH ∈ L1(A/H) as φH(xH) = H φ(xh)dh, then by the above identiﬁcation, we get FA/H(φH) = FA(φ)|H⊥, see the proof of the theorem below, which explains this technique."
  }, {
